================================================================================
## Registry without Lakebase: generic region wording
================================================================================

Context:
The SQLite registry docs, docstring and changelog named a specific cloud region
as an example of one without Lakebase. Region availability changes over time
and the example adds nothing, so the wording is now generic.

Changes:

1. changelogs/v0.9.3/hourdays_2026-11-14.log
   "not offered in every region (<region>, for example)" becomes "not offered
   in every cloud region yet".

2. docs/deployment.md
   Same rewording in "Regions without Lakebase".

3. src/back/objects/registry/store/sqlite/SQLiteRegistryStore.py
   Same rewording in the module docstring.

Modified files:
- changelogs/v0.9.3/hourdays_2026-11-14.log
- changelogs/v0.9.3/hourdays_2026-11-16.log
- docs/deployment.md
- src/back/objects/registry/store/sqlite/SQLiteRegistryStore.py

Tests: `uv run --frozen pytest -q -m "not scenario"` -> 9768 passed, 339 skipped.

================================================================================
## SQLite fallback: say "not available to this app", not "on this workspace"
================================================================================

Context:
The fallback-mode strings said Lakebase was "not available on this workspace".
A test app can run without a Lakebase binding in a region that offers Lakebase
(that is how the fallback is exercised), and the strings then made a false
claim about the region. "Not available to this app" is true in both cases.

Changes:

1. src/front/templates/base.html
   Navbar badge tooltip: "Lakebase is not available to this app".

2. src/front/templates/partials/registry/_registry_configuration.html
   Settings > Registry alert and the Lakehouse-default bullet reworded.

3. src/front/templates/partials/domain/_domain_information.html
   The disabled Lakebase card: "Not available to this app".

4. src/front/static/global/js/utils.js
   New Domain dialog: "not available to this app (SQLite fallback mode)".

5. src/shared/fastapi/health.py
   Health: "fallback mode: no Lakebase for this app".

6. src/front/fastapi/dependencies.py
   Docstring of registry_fallback().

7. tests/units/front/test_registry_fallback_flag.py
   New TestFallbackWordingIsAboutTheApp (badge, alert, card); the dialog and
   health checks assert the new wording (red before, green after).

Modified files:
- src/front/templates/base.html
- src/front/templates/partials/registry/_registry_configuration.html
- src/front/templates/partials/domain/_domain_information.html
- src/front/static/global/js/utils.js
- src/shared/fastapi/health.py
- src/front/fastapi/dependencies.py
- tests/units/front/test_registry_fallback_flag.py

Tests: `uv run --frozen pytest -q -m "not scenario"` -> 9771 passed, 339 skipped.
